    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full `BUILD SUCCESS` confirms the whole suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `locality` derivation with minimal structural impact, following the codebase's existing patterns for derived read-only owner fields:\n\n1. **`util/Localities.java`** (new) \u2014 a small, cohesive utility mirroring the existing `AddressNormalizer`/`TelephoneNormalizer` style. It holds the fixed city\u2192region table (`Sydney\u2192NSW`, `Melbourne\u2192VIC`, `Brisbane\u2192QLD`) and a single static `regionFor(city)` (CC 1) returning the canonical region or `\"UNKNOWN\"`.\n\n2. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added one `@Mapping` line to `toOwnerDto`, delegating to `Localities.regionFor(owner.getCity())`. This matches the existing expression-mapping idiom used for `displayName`, `initials`, `membershipNumber`, and `membershipTier`, so the surrounding method stays CC 1 with a single added line.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `locality` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes the field in the JSON response.\n\nAll logic lives in the new low-complexity class; the two existing files each take a tiny edit to a simple/declarative construct, keeping `changed_lines \u00d7 CC \u00d7 WMC_other` low. Tests pass (`Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 including the new `coreDerivesRegionForKnownCity` and the UNKNOWN-city case).",
